<title>USA: Lands' End authorizes buyback of more shares.</title>
<headline>Lands' End authorizes buyback of more shares.</headline>
<dateline>DODGEVILLE, Wis. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lands' End Inc said Tuesday its board of directors authorized the repurchase of up to 1.5 million additional shares of the company's common stock.</p>
<p>The company said it authorized the buyback of one million in July 1996, of which about 600,000 shares have been repurchased.  </p>
<p>The shares will be repurchased from time to time on the New York Stock Exchange or otherwise, the company said.</p>
<p>Lands' End said there were about 32.44 million shares outstanding as of today.</p>
<p>Lands' End is a direct marketer of apparel, accessories, luggage and other products.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
